- Actual-expense method: annual rent = $1,720 × 12 = $20,640. Office percentage = 165 / 780 = 11/52 ≈ 21.15%. That gives about $4,375 (20,640 × 11/52 ≈ $4,374.62) of rent allocable to the office (this is the primary example; you can also allocate a share of utilities, renter’s insurance, etc., if applicable — those increase the deduction).
- Simplified method: $5 × 165 sq ft = $825 (no Form 8829 needed).

